When the last in-flow child of a block formatting context root is a
box that margins collapse through, Ladybird collapses its top and bottom
margins together, and the root reaches past the child's border box only
by what the collapsed margin adds beyond the top margin. A line holding
text keeps margins from collapsing through its box at any height.

Blink appends both margins of a self-collapsing child to a single
MarginStrut (margin_strut.Append in BlockLayoutAlgorithm), and a new
formatting context adds that strut's Sum() to its intrinsic block size
once, at the end. WebKit tracks the same collapsed margin in its
RenderBlockFlow::MarginInfo, adds it in handleAfterSideOfBlock(), and
decides which blocks collapse through in isSelfCollapsingBlock(). Gecko
decides it with nsBlockFrame::IsEmpty() and nsLineBox::IsEmpty(), where
a text frame holding text is never empty, whatever its height.

In Chrome, the test's nine cases come out the same, and so does the
html height in each of the 40 updated expectations.
